# Trivy suppressions - reviewed 2026-09-25 (Jenkins build #4).
# Only CRITICAL findings WITH an available fix fail the Security gate. Each entry below
# has a reason and an expiry date (exp:) so it is re-reviewed automatically.

# activestorage 7.1.3.3 - path traversal / file deletion via crafted blob keys.
# Fix requires Rails >= 7.2.3 (major framework upgrade, upstream scope).
# Not exploitable here: Active Storage is loaded by rails/all but never used
# (no has_one_attached/has_many_attached, no storage service configured).
CVE-2026-33195 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-33202 exp:2026-12-31

# zlib 2.1.1 - Ruby 3.1 *default* gem shipped inside the Ruby interpreter
# (/usr/local/lib/ruby/gems/3.1.0/specifications/default). Only fixed by upgrading
# Ruby itself (see EOL Ruby accepted risk in config/brakeman.ignore).
CVE-2026-27820 exp:2026-12-31

# net-imap - the bundled gem is upgraded in Gemfile.lock (fixed). This entry covers
# the unused Ruby 3.1 *default* net-imap 0.2.4 that ships with the interpreter;
# the application loads the patched bundled version, not the default one.
CVE-2026-42257 exp:2026-12-31
